//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// A `match` whose every arm returns, missing a variant. Nothing reads the
// match's value, so the coverage check used to skip it entirely: it only ran
// when some arm ended in a tail expression. `Nothing` then fell through, the
// function ran off its end, and the caller read back whatever was in the return
// slot as a `Just`.
//
// E3028 did not catch it either -- a match whose every written arm returns
// counts as returning, and the arm that would have to return is the one that
// was not written.
//
// Found by deleting the `None` arm of `impl Clone for Option<T>` on purpose.
// That was meant to be refused and instead produced a wrong answer.
//
// `Just` is declared first so the refusal has to name the MISSING variant to
// satisfy the check. With `Nothing` first, a message that listed every variant
// would still read "does not cover Nothing" and the check would pass on a
// coverage filter that did nothing.
//
// RUN: not vxc %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: E3020
// CHECK-SAME: does not cover Nothing

enum Maybe {
  Just(i32),
  Nothing
}

fn unwrap_or_zero(m : Maybe) -> i32 {
  match m {
    Maybe::Just(v) => {
      return v;
    }
  }
}

fn main() -> i32 {
  print(unwrap_or_zero(Maybe::Nothing()));
  return 0;
}
